<title>USA: Sears says Canadian unit turns around in Q1.</title>
<headline>Sears says Canadian unit turns around in Q1.</headline>
<dateline>HOFFMAN ESTATES, Ill. 1997-04-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sears, Roebuck and Co said its Sears Canada unit experienced strong revenue increases and gross margin improvement in the first quarter.</p>
<p>Overall international operations for the quarter lost $45 million, however, compared to a $14-million loss in the same three-month period a year ago, Sears reported Thursday.</p>
<p>Two weeks ago, Sears agreed to sell controlling interest in its Sears Mexico joint venture. The retailing giant said its overall first-quarter international operations loss included a $36 million loss on the Sears Mexico sale.</p>
</text>
